  "invariants": [
    "Every lifecycle operation is capability-gated by accepted registration and compatible handshake declarations; provider names never imply support.",
    "Unsupported optional lifecycle operations return the typed capability_unsupported result and never silently fall back.",
    "All provider-local mutations carry exact coding scope, stable operation identity, deterministic idempotency, expected state generation, deadline, and live cancellation.",
    "Health is mandatory, read-only, bounded, and never infers readiness from process, socket, path, or non-empty state existence.",
    "Feedback targets exactly one stable memory reference, recall trace, or context-pack item and requires a canonically settled outcome receipt.",
    "Feedback may change provider-local learning state but never TraceDecay Native trust or another canonical authority.",
    "Maintenance is finite, bounded, single-writer per provider scope, cancellation-aware, and reports partial progress and a resume cursor.",
    "Inspection is bounded, redacted, provider-local, and cannot expose raw credentials, hidden canonical authority, or unadmitted secret material.",
    "Correction is idempotent, revision-checked, provider-local, and cannot change source code or accepted Native facts.",
    "Deletion by source has a verifiable postcondition covering remaining influence, retention locks, and every included snapshot; success cannot hide residual influence.",
    "A deleted source may not reappear in provider recall unless a new canonically admitted observation creates a new source revision.",
    "Snapshots bind provider/build/schema/scope/generation/sequence/digest identity and incompatible restore never silently resets or overwrites state.",
    "Replay consumes canonical observation receipts in monotonic sequence and reports duplicate, partial, gap, and state-generation outcomes explicitly.",
    "Provider-local explicit-fact projections and explanations remain advisory and require a separate authorized Native promotion to become canonical facts.",
    "Every success, no-effect, partial, unknown-effect, conflict, timeout, cancellation, unsupported, unavailable, or incompatible lifecycle result is typed and receipt-backed where an effect may have committed."
  ],
